window.CLEAR_CODE.register("clear/model/encoders.py",{"text":"\"\"\"encoders: scene_encoder, perception_encoder, capability_encoder, structure_encoder, kappa_set_encoder.\n\nscene_encoder: Scene encoder + object tokenizer: raw scene inputs -\u003e tokens.\n\nein notation:\n  b - batch\n  n - objects\n  s - scene tokens\n  d - model dimension\n\nperception_encoder: Perception encoder: metric terrain + embodiment -\u003e per-cell features.\n\nThis is the box the grid pipeline skipped. There, `project.classify_terrain`\nthresholded heights into FLAT/STEP/WALL with two global constants and the\nnetwork saw only the one-hot result, so it could not represent \"0.29 m ledge\"\nat all, and every body shared one classification.\n\nHere the encoder consumes metres and is conditioned on the body, because\ntraversability is a joint function of the two. The conditioning is FiLM rather\nthan a concatenated token: a wheel and a humanoid looking at the same ledge\nmust produce *different features for the same pixel*, which is a per-location\nmodulation, not a global summary another layer has to route.\n\nWhat is handed over and what is learned, deliberately:\n\n  handed over   the signed step-up to each 4-neighbour (`edge_deltas`). It is\n                an exact finite difference of the input, so making a 3x3 conv\n                rediscover it only adds an approximation error right where the\n                decision boundary is.\n\n  learned       the comparison of that step-up against the body's climb limit.\n                Feeding `limit - delta` directly would make the auxiliary head\n                trivial and measure nothing; leaving it to FiLM means the head's\n                accuracy is evidence that capability conditioning works, and\n                that evidence transfers to bodies with limits never trained on.\n\nein notation:\n  b - batch      d - channels\n  h, w - grid    e - edge directions (4)\n\ncapability_encoder: LEGACY capability encoder: the spec-sheet path. Superseded by KappaSetEncoder.\n\nThis encodes capability.feature_vector -- a fixed table of limits (terrain\nclasses, mass / extent caps, arms) handed to the model as ground truth. That\nframing is retired (2026-09-02): kappa is now a MEASURED behavioral profile --\n(probe, outcome, provenance) rows produced by the calibration instruments in\nexperiments/kappa_measure/ (rendered in experiments/kappa_arena/) and encoded\nby model/kappa_set_encoder.py, which is the default in PAMO and train_clear.\n\nThis class stays only so pre-kappa checkpoints keep loading\n(capability_encoder='vector'). Do not reach for it in new work: a spec sheet\ncannot say \"untested\", cannot carry a success RATE, and cannot grow a row\nwithout a retrain -- the three properties the measured set was built for.\n\nstructure_encoder: Row MLP and masked pooling, with the original Sequential checkpoint keys.\n\nkappa_set_encoder: KappaSetEncoder: a SET of probe observations -\u003e one capability token.\n\nDrop-in for CapabilityEncoder (same (b, 1, dim) output) but the input is\n`(probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool)` from data.probes, not a fixed\nvector. Per-probe token = Embedding(probe_id) + MLP([query, outcome]);\nmasked mean + max pooling (DeepSets) -\u003e Linear. Permutation-invariant by\nconstruction, and any subset of probes is a valid input -- that is what lets a\nmeasured robot with a missing probe, or a test-time ablation of probes, reach\nthe same planner.\n\nTraining-time probe dropout: each probe dropped with p_drop, never all of them.\nEval keeps every probe the mask allows.\n\n    python -m clear.model.kappa_set_encoder   # self-check\n\"\"\"\n\n# ---- scene_encoder ----\nimport torch\nfrom einops import rearrange\nfrom torch import nn\nfrom torch.nn import Module\n\n# constants\n\nSCENE_CHANS = 5  # flat / step / wall / start / goal\nOBJ_COLS = ('x', 'y', 'cos', 'sin', 'mass', 'extent', 's', 't', 'can_move')\nOBJ_FEAT = len(OBJ_COLS)\n\n# Columns a run can withhold, to make the model work something out instead of\n# being told it.\n#\n#   'can_move'  the ANSWER to the manipulation half of the capability question.\n#   'mass'      the harder one. can_move is just mass \u003c= max_mass, both of which\n#               are handed over, so withholding only can_move leaves a\n#               comparison between two given numbers -- which is why removing it\n#               cost about one standard deviation. Withhold mass as well and the\n#               model has to read weight off the object's shape, which the\n#               generator makes possible because crate mass is density times\n#               volume.\nDROPPABLE = ('mass', 'can_move')\n\n\ndef obj_feat_dim(drop = (), include_reachable = False):\n    return OBJ_FEAT - len(set(drop)) + int(include_reachable)\n\n\ndef object_features(poses, mass, extent, s, t, movable, grid_hw, drop = (), reachable0 = None):\n    \"\"\"Assemble (b, n, obj_feat_dim(drop, reachable0 is not None)) object features.\n\n    poses is (b, n, 3) = x, y, theta. `drop` names columns to withhold; see\n    DROPPABLE. `reachable0`: optional (b, n) bool -- is object i's own cell\n    reachable from scene.start with every OTHER object at its initial cell\n    (Example.reachable0, see data.py's own docstring on that field for why\n    this is missing signal, not decoration). None (default, every existing\n    call site) omits the column entirely -- byte-identical to before this\n    was added; only a model constructed with use_reachable=True passes it.\n    \"\"\"\n    h, w = grid_hw\n    scale = poses.new_tensor([w - 1, h - 1])\n    xy = poses[..., :2] / scale * 2 - 1\n    theta = poses[..., 2]\n    t = torch.as_tensor(t, dtype = poses.dtype, device = poses.device)\n    t = (t[:, None] if t.dim() == 1 else t).expand(s.shape)\n    cols = [\n        xy[..., 0],\n        xy[..., 1],\n        torch.cos(theta),\n        torch.sin(theta),\n        torch.log1p(mass) / 3.,\n        extent,\n        s,\n        t,\n        movable.to(poses.dtype),\n    ]\n    drop = set(drop)\n    assert drop \u003c= set(DROPPABLE), f'cannot drop {drop - set(DROPPABLE)}'\n    feats = [c for name, c in zip(OBJ_COLS, cols) if name not in drop]\n    if reachable0 is not None:\n        feats.append(reachable0.to(poses.dtype))\n    return torch.stack(feats, dim = -1)\n\n# scene encoder\n\n\nclass SceneEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Terrain / occupancy grid -\u003e a small set of spatial tokens.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, grid_hw, channels = SCENE_CHANS, stride = 2):\n        \"\"\"stride 2 (default): one token per 2x2 patch. stride 1: one token per CELL -- so a\n        terrain token is a single cell's ground, not a pooled patch (PriorityHead scene_stride).\"\"\"\n        super().__init__()\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(channels, dim // 2, 3, padding = 1),\n            nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv2d(dim // 2, dim, 3, stride = stride, padding = 1),\n            nn.GELU(),\n        )\n        h, w = grid_hw\n        self.stride = stride\n        self.num_tokens = ((h + stride - 1) // stride) * ((w + stride - 1) // stride)\n        self.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, self.num_tokens, dim))\n\n    def forward(self, grid):\n        tokens = rearrange(self.net(grid), 'b d h w -\u003e b (h w) d')\n        return tokens + self.pos_emb\n\n\ndef grow_scene_channels(state_dict, new_channels, prefixes = (\"priority_head.scene_encoder\",\n                                                              \"velocity_field.scene_encoder\")):\n    \"\"\"Widen a checkpoint's scene-encoder input conv from C to `new_channels`.\n\n    The extra channels are initialised to ZERO, so the grown model computes\n    EXACTLY what the original did on its first forward pass and then learns to\n    use the new inputs -- the same reason CrossTracer initialises its FiLM\n    layers near identity. A random init here would instead throw away the\n    trained representation the moment the ego channels are attached, which is\n    indistinguishable from \"the ego channels hurt\" when the run is scored.\n\n    Relies on the channel contract in `data/ego_project.py`: the five class\n    channels stay FIRST, so `w[:, :C]` keeps its meaning. Reordering them would\n    silently mis-wire every grown checkpoint.\n\n    -\u003e (state_dict, [names of the tensors that were widened]). Mutates a copy.\n    \"\"\"\n    out, grown = dict(state_dict), []\n    for pre in prefixes:\n        key = f\"{pre}.net.0.weight\"\n        if key not in out:\n            continue\n        w = out[key]\n        c = w.shape[1]\n        if c == new_channels:\n            continue\n        if c \u003e new_channels:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{key} has {c} channels, cannot shrink to {new_channels}\")\n        wide = w.new_zeros((w.shape[0], new_channels) + tuple(w.shape[2:]))\n        wide[:, :c] = w\n        out[key] = wide\n        grown.append(key)\n    return out, grown\n\n\nclass MetricSceneEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Perception features -\u003e spatial tokens, for the metric-terrain path.\n\n    SceneEncoder above takes the 5-channel class grid and is what the grid\n    experiments train on. This one takes what PerceptionEncoder produced --\n    per-cell features that already know the height field AND the body looking\n    at it -- and only does the pooling into tokens.\n\n    Keeping the two separate rather than adding a flag: they consume different\n    worlds, and a shared class whose first line branches on which is a merge\n    conflict waiting for the day the class grid is deleted.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, grid_hw, in_dim):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.proj = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(in_dim, dim, 3, stride = 2, padding = 1),\n            nn.GELU(),\n        )\n        h, w = grid_hw\n        self.num_tokens = ((h + 1) // 2) * ((w + 1) // 2)\n        self.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, self.num_tokens, dim))\n\n    def forward(self, features):\n        tokens = rearrange(self.proj(features), 'b d h w -\u003e b (h w) d')\n        return tokens + self.pos_emb\n\n\n# ---- perception_encoder ----\nfrom clear.data.terrain import EDGES, OFF_GRID_STEP\n\n# input channel budget: height, 4 edge deltas, occupancy, start, goal\nPERCEPT_CHANS = 1 + len(EDGES) + 3\n\n# metres; real terrain tops out at 1.0 m (mj_maze wall slabs). Off-grid edges\n# arrive as a large sentinel -- clamping keeps them distinctly \"unclimbable\"\n# without letting one channel dominate the input scale.\nHEIGHT_CLAMP = 1.5\n\n\ndef edge_deltas_torch(heights):\n    \"\"\"(b, h, w) metric heights -\u003e (b, 4, h, w) signed step-up per neighbour.\n\n    Mirrors data.terrain.edge_deltas exactly (same EDGES order, same off-grid\n    sentinel) so labels and inputs cannot drift apart; tests/test_perception.py\n    asserts they agree elementwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    b, h, w = heights.shape\n    out = heights.new_empty((b, len(EDGES), h, w))\n    for k, (dr, dc) in enumerate(EDGES):\n        nb = heights.new_full((b, h, w), OFF_GRID_STEP)\n        r0, r1 = max(0, -dr), h - max(0, dr)\n        c0, c1 = max(0, -dc), w - max(0, dc)\n        nb[:, r0:r1, c0:c1] = heights[:, r0 + dr:r1 + dr, c0 + dc:c1 + dc]\n        out[:, k] = nb - heights\n    return out\n\n\ndef perception_input(heights, occupancy, start, goal):\n    \"\"\"Assemble (b, PERCEPT_CHANS, h, w). All inputs are (b, h, w).\"\"\"\n    deltas = edge_deltas_torch(heights).clamp(-HEIGHT_CLAMP, HEIGHT_CLAMP)\n    return torch.cat([\n        (heights / HEIGHT_CLAMP)[:, None],\n        deltas / HEIGHT_CLAMP,\n        occupancy[:, None].to(heights.dtype),\n        start[:, None].to(heights.dtype),\n        goal[:, None].to(heights.dtype),\n    ], dim = 1)\n\n\nclass FiLM(Module):\n    \"\"\"Per-channel affine modulation from the capability vector.\n\n    Zero-initialised so the encoder starts as the unconditioned network and\n    conditioning is something it acquires -- the same reason the AdaLN blocks\n    in the dynamics flow start at identity. A randomly initialised FiLM\n    multiplies early features by noise that depends on the body, which reads\n    to the optimiser as label noise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, cap_dim, channels):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.to_scale_shift = nn.Linear(cap_dim, channels * 2)\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.to_scale_shift.weight)\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.to_scale_shift.bias)\n\n    def forward(self, x, cap):\n        scale, shift = self.to_scale_shift(cap).chunk(2, dim = -1)\n        return x * (1.0 + scale[..., None, None]) + shift[..., None, None]\n\n\nclass PerceptionEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"(heights, occupancy, start, goal, capability) -\u003e (b, dim, h, w) features\n    plus per-edge traversability logits.\n\n    The auxiliary head is not decoration. Scene success is a single number at\n    the end of a long pipeline; per-edge traversability is dense, exactly\n    supervised, and fails loudly the moment capability conditioning stops\n    working. Train with it, read it, and only then trust the rest.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, cap_dim, depth = 3, in_chans = PERCEPT_CHANS,\n                 cond = 'film'):\n        super().__init__()\n        assert cond in ('film', 'concat'), cond\n        # 'concat' is the ablation: the same capability vector broadcast as\n        # constant input channels, i.e. told once at the input instead of at\n        # every layer and location. Keeping it here rather than in a fork means\n        # the two share every other line, so a difference is the conditioning.\n        self.cond = cond\n        self.cap_dim = cap_dim\n        self.stem = nn.Conv2d(in_chans + (cap_dim if cond == 'concat' else 0),\n                              dim, 3, padding = 1)\n        self.blocks = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.films = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.norms = nn.ModuleList()\n        for _ in range(depth):\n            self.blocks.append(nn.Conv2d(dim, dim, 3, padding = 1))\n            self.norms.append(nn.GroupNorm(min(8, dim), dim))\n            self.films.append(FiLM(cap_dim, dim))\n        self.act = nn.GELU()\n        self.stem_film = FiLM(cap_dim, dim)\n        self.edge_head = nn.Conv2d(dim, len(EDGES), 1)\n\n    def forward(self, heights, occupancy, start, goal, cap):\n        inp = perception_input(heights, occupancy, start, goal)\n        if self.cond == 'concat':\n            b, _, h, w = inp.shape\n            inp = torch.cat([inp, cap[:, :, None, None].expand(b, self.cap_dim, h, w)], 1)\n            x = self.act(self.stem(inp))\n            for conv, norm in zip(self.blocks, self.norms):\n                x = x + self.act(norm(conv(x)))\n        else:\n            x = self.act(self.stem_film(self.stem(inp), cap))\n            for conv, norm, film in zip(self.blocks, self.norms, self.films):\n                x = x + self.act(film(norm(conv(x)), cap))\n        return x, self.edge_head(x)\n\n\n# ---- capability_encoder ----\nfrom clear.data.capability import FEATURE_DIM, PHYSICAL_DIM\n\n\nclass CapabilityEncoder(Module):\n    def __init__(self, dim, feature_dim = FEATURE_DIM):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.to_token = nn.Linear(feature_dim, dim)\n\n    def forward(self, capability):\n        \"\"\"(b, feature_dim) -\u003e (b, 1, d) embodiment token.\"\"\"\n        return self.to_token(capability)[:, None, :]\n\n\nclass SensitivityHead(Module):\n    \"\"\"Hard-example reweighting for physical-cost loss terms -- iteration 2,\n    superseding the CrossTracer-style learned-per-embodiment-MLP version\n    (arXiv 2601's \"Embodiment Sensitivity Head\" -- see\n    docs/RESEARCH_coins_crosstracer_ordering.md for the full history).\n\n    Read by PAMO.forward() (learned_loss_weight=True) to replace the single\n    hand-tuned endpoint_weight/validity_weight constant, shared across every\n    example, with a per-object multiplier -- see clear.py's own comment on\n    those constants pulling in opposite directions for discrete vs\n    continuous.\n\n    **Why this isn't `alpha_e = f(emb_feat)` any more.** Two iterations of\n    that design (unbounded Softplus, then bounded-via-tanh to [0.5, 1.5])\n    both collapsed to the SAME degenerate pattern in every seed tested: two\n    of the three embodiments pinned at the minimum weight, one at the\n    maximum. Root cause, confirmed by measuring per-embodiment endpoint\n    error directly on an unbiased checkpoint (`runs/llw_ablation/\n    llw_base_seed0`): wheel=0.0501, quadruped=0.0173, humanoid=0.0042 --\n    the head was upweighting whichever embodiment ALREADY had the LOWEST\n    error, not the highest. This is not a tuning problem, it's structural:\n    for a normalized weighted mean `L = sum(alpha_i * err_i) / sum(alpha_i)`,\n    `dL/d(alpha_i) ~ (err_i - L)`, so gradient descent on `alpha` (however\n    it's parameterized, learned from emb_feat or anything else) always\n    increases weight on below-average-error terms and decreases it on\n    above-average ones -- exactly backwards from \"pay more attention to\n    what's hard\", regardless of how tightly alpha is bounded.\n\n    **This version has no learned parameters at all**, precisely because a\n    learned function of anything, trained end-to-end against this same\n    normalized loss, inherits the same backwards incentive. Instead, alpha\n    is a direct, monotonically INCREASING function of each object's own\n    CURRENT error, ALREADY-DETACHED by the caller before it reaches here --\n    the classic hard-example-reweighting / OHEM / focal-loss recipe. With\n    no free parameters, there is nothing left for gradient descent to game.\n    \"\"\"\n    MAX_DEV = 0.5  # alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV] -- same bound as the superseded\n    # learned version, kept for comparability; not itself what fixes the incentive here.\n\n    def forward(self, err, movable):\n        \"\"\"err: (b, n) per-object error the caller has ALREADY detached (this\n        function never calls .detach() itself -- the caller decides what\n        \"error\" means, endpoint error today). movable: (b, n) bool.\n        -\u003e (b, n) alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV], centered on the\n        batch's own mean movable-object error (an average-error object gets\n        alpha == 1.0; above-average gets \u003e 1.0; below-average gets \u003c 1.0).\"\"\"\n        mv = movable.to(err.dtype)\n        n = mv.sum().clamp(min = 1.0)\n        mean = (err * mv).sum() / n\n        var = (((err - mean) ** 2) * mv).sum() / n\n        std = var.clamp(min = 1e-8).sqrt()\n        z = (err - mean) / std\n        return 1.0 + self.MAX_DEV * torch.tanh(z)\n\n\nclass MorphCapabilityEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Link rows -\u003e (conditioning vector, token): kappa = e(morphology) for the\n    metric front end (docs/PREREGISTRATION_learned_ccor_2026-09-02.md follow-up).\n\n    Same output contract as PhysicalCapabilityEncoder -- a cap_dim vector that\n    FiLMs perception and a (b, 1, dim) token for the transformer -- but the\n    input is (morph_rows, morph_mask) from data/morphology.py, so the body's\n    STRUCTURE is the only capability channel; no limit is ever handed over.\n    The token comes from the adopted v1 set-attention MorphologyEncoder\n    (EXPERIMENT_morph_kappa_2026-09-02.md); the conditioning vector is a linear\n    read of that token.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, cap_dim = 64, hidden = 128, depth = 2, heads = 4,\n                 p_drop = 0.15):\n        super().__init__()\n        from clear.model.morphology_encoder import MorphologyEncoder\n        self.enc = MorphologyEncoder(dim, hidden = hidden, depth = depth,\n                                     heads = heads, p_drop = p_drop)\n        self.to_cap = nn.Linear(dim, cap_dim)\n        self.cap_dim = cap_dim\n\n    def forward(self, capability):\n        \"\"\"((b, L, F) rows, (b, L) mask) -\u003e ((b, cap_dim), (b, 1, dim)).\"\"\"\n        tok = self.enc(capability)\n        return self.to_cap(tok[:, 0]), tok\n\n\nclass PhysicalCapabilityEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Metric descriptor -\u003e (conditioning vector, token).\n\n    Separate from CapabilityEncoder above because it answers a different\n    question. That one summarises a body for the ordering transformer, where a\n    single token attended over is enough. This one drives FiLM inside the\n    perception encoder, where the body has to change how a *pixel* is read --\n    so it produces a vector consumed at every spatial location, and a token for\n    the transformer as a by-product.\n\n    The input is capability.physical_vector: metres and kilograms, no class\n    membership. That is what makes an unseen climb limit a valid input rather\n    than an out-of-vocabulary one.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, cap_dim = 64, feature_dim = PHYSICAL_DIM):\n        super().__init__()\n        # climb is in metres and everything else is already O(1); normalise the\n        # first channel here rather than at every call site.\n        self.register_buffer('scale', torch.tensor(\n            [1.0 / HEIGHT_CLAMP] + [1.0] * (feature_dim - 1), dtype = torch.float32))\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(feature_dim, cap_dim), nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Linear(cap_dim, cap_dim),\n        )\n        self.to_token = nn.Linear(cap_dim, dim)\n        self.cap_dim = cap_dim\n\n    def forward(self, physical):\n        \"\"\"(b, feature_dim) -\u003e ((b, cap_dim) conditioning, (b, 1, dim) token).\"\"\"\n        cap = self.net(physical * self.scale)\n        return cap, self.to_token(cap)[:, None, :]\n\n\n# ---- structure_encoder ----\nclass StructureEncoder(nn.Sequential):\n    def __init__(self, input_dim, dim):\n        super().__init__(nn.Linear(input_dim, dim), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(dim, dim))\n\n    def pool(self, structure, structure_mask):\n        rows = self(structure)\n        mask = structure_mask[..., None].to(rows.dtype)\n        return (rows * mask).sum(1) / mask.sum(1).clamp(min=1)\n\n\n# ---- kappa_set_encoder ----\nclass KappaSetEncoder(Module):\n    def __init__(self, dim, n_probes = 10, p_drop = 0.3, hidden = 64):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.p_drop = p_drop\n        self.id_embed = nn.Embedding(n_probes, hidden)\n        self.val_mlp = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(2, hidden), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(hidden, hidden))\n        self.to_token = nn.Linear(2 * hidden, dim)\n\n    def forward(self, capability):\n        \"\"\"capability = (probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool) -\u003e (b, 1, dim).\"\"\"\n        probes, mask = capability\n        mask = mask.bool()\n        if self.training and self.p_drop \u003e 0:\n            keep = torch.rand(mask.shape, device = mask.device) \u003e= self.p_drop\n            keep = keep \u0026 mask\n            # never drop every probe: fall back to the original mask for those rows\n            empty = ~keep.any(dim = 1, keepdim = True)\n            mask = torch.where(empty, mask, keep)\n        tok = self.id_embed(probes[..., 0].long()) + self.val_mlp(probes[..., 1:3])  # (b, P, h)\n        m = mask[..., None].to(tok.dtype)\n        mean = (tok * m).sum(1) / m.sum(1).clamp(min = 1.0)\n        mx = tok.masked_fill(~mask[..., None], float('-inf')).amax(1)\n        mx = torch.where(torch.isfinite(mx), mx, torch.zeros_like(mx))  # all-masked row -\u003e 0\n        return self.to_token(torch.cat([mean, mx], dim = -1))[:, None, :]\n\n\ndef _self_check():\n    torch.manual_seed(0)\n    enc = KappaSetEncoder(32, n_probes = 10, p_drop = 0.3).eval()\n    b, P = 4, 10\n    probes = torch.stack([torch.arange(P).float(), torch.rand(P), torch.rand(P).round()], -1)[None].repeat(b, 1, 1)\n    mask = torch.ones(b, P, dtype = torch.bool)\n    out = enc((probes, mask))\n    assert out.shape == (b, 1, 32), out.shape\n    perm = torch.randperm(P)\n    out_p = enc((probes[:, perm], mask[:, perm]))\n    assert torch.allclose(out, out_p, atol = 1e-5), \"not permutation invariant\"\n    # mask handling: masking probe 3 == physically removing it\n    mask2 = mask.clone(); mask2[:, 3] = False\n    keep = [i for i in range(P) if i != 3]\n    a = enc((probes, mask2)); c = enc((probes[:, keep], mask[:, keep]))\n    assert torch.allclose(a, c, atol = 1e-5), \"masked probe leaks into the token\"\n    assert not torch.allclose(a, out, atol = 1e-3), \"removing a probe changed nothing\"\n    # training drop never empties a row\n    enc.train()\n    for _ in range(20):\n        o = enc((probes, mask))\n        assert torch.isfinite(o).all()\n    print(\"ok KappaSetEncoder: shape (b,1,dim), permutation-invariant, mask == removal, drop finite\")\n","lines":["\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;encoders: scene_encoder, perception_encoder, capability_encoder, structure_encoder, kappa_set_encoder.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003escene_encoder: Scene encoder + object tokenizer: raw scene inputs -\u0026gt; tokens.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eein notation:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  b - batch\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  n - objects\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  s - scene tokens\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  d - model dimension\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eperception_encoder: Perception encoder: metric terrain + embodiment -\u0026gt; per-cell features.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eThis is the box the grid pipeline skipped. There, `project.classify_terrain`\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ethresholded heights into FLAT/STEP/WALL with two global constants and the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003enetwork saw only the one-hot result, so it could not represent \u0026quot;0.29 m ledge\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eat all, and every body shared one classification.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eHere the encoder consumes metres and is conditioned on the body, because\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003etraversability is a joint function of the two. The conditioning is FiLM rather\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ethan a concatenated token: a wheel and a humanoid looking at the same ledge\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emust produce *different features for the same pixel*, which is a per-location\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emodulation, not a global summary another layer has to route.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eWhat is handed over and what is learned, deliberately:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  handed over   the signed step-up to each 4-neighbour (`edge_deltas`). It is\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                an exact finite difference of the input, so making a 3x3 conv\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                rediscover it only adds an approximation error right where the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                decision boundary is.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  learned       the comparison of that step-up against the body\u0026#x27;s climb limit.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                Feeding `limit - delta` directly would make the auxiliary head\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                trivial and measure nothing; leaving it to FiLM means the head\u0026#x27;s\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                accuracy is evidence that capability conditioning works, and\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                that evidence transfers to bodies with limits never trained on.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eein notation:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  b - batch      d - channels\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  h, w - grid    e - edge directions (4)\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ecapability_encoder: LEGACY capability encoder: the spec-sheet path. Superseded by KappaSetEncoder.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eThis encodes capability.feature_vector -- a fixed table of limits (terrain\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eclasses, mass / extent caps, arms) handed to the model as ground truth. That\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eframing is retired (2026-09-02): kappa is now a MEASURED behavioral profile --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e(probe, outcome, provenance) rows produced by the calibration instruments in\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eexperiments/kappa_measure/ (rendered in experiments/kappa_arena/) and encoded\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eby model/kappa_set_encoder.py, which is the default in PAMO and train_clear.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eThis class stays only so pre-kappa checkpoints keep loading\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e(capability_encoder=\u0026#x27;vector\u0026#x27;). Do not reach for it in new work: a spec sheet\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ecannot say \u0026quot;untested\u0026quot;, cannot carry a success RATE, and cannot grow a row\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ewithout a retrain -- the three properties the measured set was built for.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003estructure_encoder: Row MLP and masked pooling, with the original Sequential checkpoint keys.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ekappa_set_encoder: KappaSetEncoder: a SET of probe observations -\u0026gt; one capability token.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eDrop-in for CapabilityEncoder (same (b, 1, dim) output) but the input is\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e`(probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool)` from data.probes, not a fixed\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003evector. Per-probe token = Embedding(probe_id) + MLP([query, outcome]);\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emasked mean + max pooling (DeepSets) -\u0026gt; Linear. Permutation-invariant by\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003econstruction, and any subset of probes is a valid input -- that is what lets a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emeasured robot with a missing probe, or a test-time ablation of probes, reach\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ethe same planner.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eTraining-time probe dropout: each probe dropped with p_drop, never all of them.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eEval keeps every probe the mask allows.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    python -m clear.model.kappa_set_encoder   # self-check\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- scene_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e torch","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e einops \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e rearrange","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e torch \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e nn","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e torch.nn \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e Module","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# constants\u003c/span\u003e","","SCENE_CHANS = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e5\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# flat / step / wall / start / goal\u003c/span\u003e","OBJ_COLS = (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;x\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;y\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;cos\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;sin\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;mass\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;extent\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;s\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;t\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;can_move\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e)","OBJ_FEAT = len(OBJ_COLS)","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# Columns a run can withhold, to make the model work something out instead of\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# being told it.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#   \u0026#x27;can_move\u0026#x27;  the ANSWER to the manipulation half of the capability question.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#   \u0026#x27;mass\u0026#x27;      the harder one. can_move is just mass \u0026lt;= max_mass, both of which\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               are handed over, so withholding only can_move leaves a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               comparison between two given numbers -- which is why removing it\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               cost about one standard deviation. Withhold mass as well and the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               model has to read weight off the object\u0026#x27;s shape, which the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               generator makes possible because crate mass is density times\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               volume.\u003c/span\u003e","DROPPABLE = (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;mass\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;can_move\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eobj_feat_dim\u003c/span\u003e(drop = (), include_reachable = \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e OBJ_FEAT - len(set(drop)) + int(include_reachable)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eobject_features\u003c/span\u003e(poses, mass, extent, s, t, movable, grid_hw, drop = (), reachable0 = \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Assemble (b, n, obj_feat_dim(drop, reachable0 is not None)) object features.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    poses is (b, n, 3) = x, y, theta. `drop` names columns to withhold; see\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    DROPPABLE. `reachable0`: optional (b, n) bool -- is object i\u0026#x27;s own cell\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    reachable from scene.start with every OTHER object at its initial cell\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    (Example.reachable0, see data.py\u0026#x27;s own docstring on that field for why\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    this is missing signal, not decoration). None (default, every existing\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    call site) omits the column entirely -- byte-identical to before this\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    was added; only a model constructed with use_reachable=True passes it.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    h, w = grid_hw","    scale = poses.new_tensor([w - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, h - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e])","    xy = poses[..., :\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e] / scale * \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e","    theta = poses[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e]","    t = torch.as_tensor(t, dtype = poses.dtype, device = poses.device)","    t = (t[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e] \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e t.dim() == \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e t).expand(s.shape)","    cols = [","        xy[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e],","        xy[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e],","        torch.cos(theta),","        torch.sin(theta),","        torch.log1p(mass) / \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3.\u003c/span\u003e,","        extent,","        s,","        t,","        movable.to(poses.dtype),","    ]","    drop = set(drop)","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e drop \u0026lt;= set(DROPPABLE), f\u0026#x27;cannot drop {drop - set(DROPPABLE)}\u0026#x27;","    feats = [c \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e name, c \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e zip(OBJ_COLS, cols) \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e name \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e drop]","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e reachable0 \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e:","        feats.append(reachable0.to(poses.dtype))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e torch.stack(feats, dim = -\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# scene encoder\u003c/span\u003e","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eSceneEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Terrain / occupancy grid -\u0026gt; a small set of spatial tokens.\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, grid_hw, channels = SCENE_CHANS, stride = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;stride 2 (default): one token per 2x2 patch. stride 1: one token per CELL -- so a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        terrain token is a single cell\u0026#x27;s ground, not a pooled patch (PriorityHead scene_stride).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Conv2d(channels, dim // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, padding = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e),","            nn.GELU(),","            nn.Conv2d(dim // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, stride = stride, padding = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e),","            nn.GELU(),","        )","        h, w = grid_hw","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stride = stride","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens = ((h + stride - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // stride) * ((w + stride - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // stride)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens, dim))","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, grid):","        tokens = rearrange(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net(grid), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;b d h w -\u0026gt; b (h w) d\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e tokens + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003egrow_scene_channels\u003c/span\u003e(state_dict, new_channels, prefixes = (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;priority_head.scene_encoder\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e,","                                                              \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;velocity_field.scene_encoder\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Widen a checkpoint\u0026#x27;s scene-encoder input conv from C to `new_channels`.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The extra channels are initialised to ZERO, so the grown model computes\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    EXACTLY what the original did on its first forward pass and then learns to\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    use the new inputs -- the same reason CrossTracer initialises its FiLM\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    layers near identity. A random init here would instead throw away the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    trained representation the moment the ego channels are attached, which is\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    indistinguishable from \u0026quot;the ego channels hurt\u0026quot; when the run is scored.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Relies on the channel contract in `data/ego_project.py`: the five class\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    channels stay FIRST, so `w[:, :C]` keeps its meaning. Reordering them would\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    silently mis-wire every grown checkpoint.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    -\u0026gt; (state_dict, [names of the tensors that were widened]). Mutates a copy.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    out, grown = dict(state_dict), []","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e pre \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e prefixes:","        key = f\u0026quot;{pre}.net.0.weight\u0026quot;","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e key \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e out:","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003econtinue\u003c/span\u003e","        w = out[key]","        c = w.shape[\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e]","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e c == new_channels:","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003econtinue\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e c \u0026gt; new_channels:","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eraise\u003c/span\u003e ValueError(f\u0026quot;{key} has {c} channels, cannot shrink to {new_channels}\u0026quot;)","        wide = w.new_zeros((w.shape[\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e], new_channels) + tuple(w.shape[\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e:]))","        wide[:, :c] = w","        out[key] = wide","        grown.append(key)","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e out, grown","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eMetricSceneEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Perception features -\u0026gt; spatial tokens, for the metric-terrain path.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    SceneEncoder above takes the 5-channel class grid and is what the grid\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    experiments train on. This one takes what PerceptionEncoder produced --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    per-cell features that already know the height field AND the body looking\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    at it -- and only does the pooling into tokens.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Keeping the two separate rather than adding a flag: they consume different\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    worlds, and a shared class whose first line branches on which is a merge\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    conflict waiting for the day the class grid is deleted.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, grid_hw, in_dim):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.proj = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Conv2d(in_dim, dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, stride = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, padding = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e),","            nn.GELU(),","        )","        h, w = grid_hw","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens = ((h + \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e) * ((w + \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens, dim))","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, features):","        tokens = rearrange(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.proj(features), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;b d h w -\u0026gt; b (h w) d\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e tokens + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- perception_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e clear.data.terrain \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e EDGES, OFF_GRID_STEP","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# input channel budget: height, 4 edge deltas, occupancy, start, goal\u003c/span\u003e","PERCEPT_CHANS = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e + len(EDGES) + \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# metres; real terrain tops out at 1.0 m (mj_maze wall slabs). Off-grid edges\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# arrive as a large sentinel -- clamping keeps them distinctly \u0026quot;unclimbable\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# without letting one channel dominate the input scale.\u003c/span\u003e","HEIGHT_CLAMP = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.5\u003c/span\u003e","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eedge_deltas_torch\u003c/span\u003e(heights):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(b, h, w) metric heights -\u0026gt; (b, 4, h, w) signed step-up per neighbour.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Mirrors data.terrain.edge_deltas exactly (same EDGES order, same off-grid\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    sentinel) so labels and inputs cannot drift apart; tests/test_perception.py\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    asserts they agree elementwise.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    b, h, w = heights.shape","    out = heights.new_empty((b, len(EDGES), h, w))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e k, (dr, dc) \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e enumerate(EDGES):","        nb = heights.new_full((b, h, w), OFF_GRID_STEP)","        r0, r1 = max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, -dr), h - max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, dr)","        c0, c1 = max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, -dc), w - max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, dc)","        nb[:, r0:r1, c0:c1] = heights[:, r0 + dr:r1 + dr, c0 + dc:c1 + dc]","        out[:, k] = nb - heights","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e out","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eperception_input\u003c/span\u003e(heights, occupancy, start, goal):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Assemble (b, PERCEPT_CHANS, h, w). All inputs are (b, h, w).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    deltas = edge_deltas_torch(heights).clamp(-HEIGHT_CLAMP, HEIGHT_CLAMP)","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e torch.cat([","        (heights / HEIGHT_CLAMP)[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e],","        deltas / HEIGHT_CLAMP,","        occupancy[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(heights.dtype),","        start[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(heights.dtype),","        goal[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(heights.dtype),","    ], dim = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eFiLM\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Per-channel affine modulation from the capability vector.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Zero-initialised so the encoder starts as the unconditioned network and\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    conditioning is something it acquires -- the same reason the AdaLN blocks\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    in the dynamics flow start at identity. A randomly initialised FiLM\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    multiplies early features by noise that depends on the body, which reads\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    to the optimiser as label noise.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, cap_dim, channels):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift = nn.Linear(cap_dim, channels * \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e)","        nn.init.zeros_(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift.weight)","        nn.init.zeros_(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift.bias)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, x, cap):","        scale, shift = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift(cap).chunk(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, dim = -\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e x * (\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e + scale[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e]) + shift[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003ePerceptionEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(heights, occupancy, start, goal, capability) -\u0026gt; (b, dim, h, w) features\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    plus per-edge traversability logits.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The auxiliary head is not decoration. Scene success is a single number at\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the end of a long pipeline; per-edge traversability is dense, exactly\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    supervised, and fails loudly the moment capability conditioning stops\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    working. Train with it, read it, and only then trust the rest.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, cap_dim, depth = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, in_chans = PERCEPT_CHANS,","                 cond = \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;film\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e cond \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;film\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;concat\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e), cond","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# \u0026#x27;concat\u0026#x27; is the ablation: the same capability vector broadcast as\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# constant input channels, i.e. told once at the input instead of at\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# every layer and location. Keeping it here rather than in a fork means\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# the two share every other line, so a difference is the conditioning.\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cond = cond","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim = cap_dim","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem = nn.Conv2d(in_chans + (cap_dim \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e cond == \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;concat\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e),","                              dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, padding = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks = nn.ModuleList()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.films = nn.ModuleList()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms = nn.ModuleList()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e _ \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e range(depth):","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks.append(nn.Conv2d(dim, dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, padding = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms.append(nn.GroupNorm(min(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e8\u003c/span\u003e, dim), dim))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.films.append(FiLM(cap_dim, dim))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act = nn.GELU()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem_film = FiLM(cap_dim, dim)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.edge_head = nn.Conv2d(dim, len(EDGES), \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, heights, occupancy, start, goal, cap):","        inp = perception_input(heights, occupancy, start, goal)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cond == \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;concat\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e:","            b, _, h, w = inp.shape","            inp = torch.cat([inp, cap[:, :, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].expand(b, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim, h, w)], \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","            x = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem(inp))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e conv, norm \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e zip(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms):","                x = x + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(norm(conv(x)))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e:","            x = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem_film(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem(inp), cap))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e conv, norm, film \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e zip(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.films):","                x = x + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(film(norm(conv(x)), cap))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e x, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.edge_head(x)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- capability_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e clear.data.capability \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e FEATURE_DIM, PHYSICAL_DIM","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eCapabilityEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, feature_dim = FEATURE_DIM):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token = nn.Linear(feature_dim, dim)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, capability):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(b, feature_dim) -\u0026gt; (b, 1, d) embodiment token.\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token(capability)[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, :]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eSensitivityHead\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Hard-example reweighting for physical-cost loss terms -- iteration 2,\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    superseding the CrossTracer-style learned-per-embodiment-MLP version\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    (arXiv 2601\u0026#x27;s \u0026quot;Embodiment Sensitivity Head\u0026quot; -- see\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    docs/RESEARCH_coins_crosstracer_ordering.md for the full history).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Read by PAMO.forward() (learned_loss_weight=True) to replace the single\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    hand-tuned endpoint_weight/validity_weight constant, shared across every\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    example, with a per-object multiplier -- see clear.py\u0026#x27;s own comment on\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    those constants pulling in opposite directions for discrete vs\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    continuous.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    **Why this isn\u0026#x27;t `alpha_e = f(emb_feat)` any more.** Two iterations of\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    that design (unbounded Softplus, then bounded-via-tanh to [0.5, 1.5])\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    both collapsed to the SAME degenerate pattern in every seed tested: two\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    of the three embodiments pinned at the minimum weight, one at the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    maximum. Root cause, confirmed by measuring per-embodiment endpoint\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    error directly on an unbiased checkpoint (`runs/llw_ablation/\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    llw_base_seed0`): wheel=0.0501, quadruped=0.0173, humanoid=0.0042 --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the head was upweighting whichever embodiment ALREADY had the LOWEST\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    error, not the highest. This is not a tuning problem, it\u0026#x27;s structural:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    for a normalized weighted mean `L = sum(alpha_i * err_i) / sum(alpha_i)`,\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    `dL/d(alpha_i) ~ (err_i - L)`, so gradient descent on `alpha` (however\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    it\u0026#x27;s parameterized, learned from emb_feat or anything else) always\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    increases weight on below-average-error terms and decreases it on\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    above-average ones -- exactly backwards from \u0026quot;pay more attention to\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    what\u0026#x27;s hard\u0026quot;, regardless of how tightly alpha is bounded.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    **This version has no learned parameters at all**, precisely because a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    learned function of anything, trained end-to-end against this same\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    normalized loss, inherits the same backwards incentive. Instead, alpha\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    is a direct, monotonically INCREASING function of each object\u0026#x27;s own\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    CURRENT error, ALREADY-DETACHED by the caller before it reaches here --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the classic hard-example-reweighting / OHEM / focal-loss recipe. With\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    no free parameters, there is nothing left for gradient descent to game.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    MAX_DEV = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.5\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV] -- same bound as the superseded\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# learned version, kept for comparability; not itself what fixes the incentive here.\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, err, movable):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;err: (b, n) per-object error the caller has ALREADY detached (this\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        function never calls .detach() itself -- the caller decides what\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        \u0026quot;error\u0026quot; means, endpoint error today). movable: (b, n) bool.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        -\u0026gt; (b, n) alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV], centered on the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        batch\u0026#x27;s own mean movable-object error (an average-error object gets\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        alpha == 1.0; above-average gets \u0026gt; 1.0; below-average gets \u0026lt; 1.0).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        mv = movable.to(err.dtype)","        n = mv.sum().clamp(min = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e)","        mean = (err * mv).sum() / n","        var = (((err - mean) ** \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e) * mv).sum() / n","        std = var.clamp(min = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-8\u003c/span\u003e).sqrt()","        z = (err - mean) / std","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.MAX_DEV * torch.tanh(z)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eMorphCapabilityEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Link rows -\u0026gt; (conditioning vector, token): kappa = e(morphology) for the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    metric front end (docs/PREREGISTRATION_learned_ccor_2026-09-02.md follow-up).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Same output contract as PhysicalCapabilityEncoder -- a cap_dim vector that\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    FiLMs perception and a (b, 1, dim) token for the transformer -- but the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    input is (morph_rows, morph_mask) from data/morphology.py, so the body\u0026#x27;s\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    STRUCTURE is the only capability channel; no limit is ever handed over.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The token comes from the adopted v1 set-attention MorphologyEncoder\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    (EXPERIMENT_morph_kappa_2026-09-02.md); the conditioning vector is a linear\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    read of that token.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, cap_dim = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e, hidden = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e128\u003c/span\u003e, depth = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, heads = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e,","                 p_drop = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.15\u003c/span\u003e):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e clear.model.morphology_encoder \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e MorphologyEncoder","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.enc = MorphologyEncoder(dim, hidden = hidden, depth = depth,","                                     heads = heads, p_drop = p_drop)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_cap = nn.Linear(dim, cap_dim)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim = cap_dim","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, capability):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;((b, L, F) rows, (b, L) mask) -\u0026gt; ((b, cap_dim), (b, 1, dim)).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        tok = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.enc(capability)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_cap(tok[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e]), tok","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003ePhysicalCapabilityEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Metric descriptor -\u0026gt; (conditioning vector, token).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Separate from CapabilityEncoder above because it answers a different\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    question. That one summarises a body for the ordering transformer, where a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    single token attended over is enough. This one drives FiLM inside the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    perception encoder, where the body has to change how a *pixel* is read --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    so it produces a vector consumed at every spatial location, and a token for\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the transformer as a by-product.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The input is capability.physical_vector: metres and kilograms, no class\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    membership. That is what makes an unseen climb limit a valid input rather\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    than an out-of-vocabulary one.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, cap_dim = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e, feature_dim = PHYSICAL_DIM):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# climb is in metres and everything else is already O(1); normalise the\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# first channel here rather than at every call site.\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.register_buffer(\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;scale\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e, torch.tensor(","            [\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e / HEIGHT_CLAMP] + [\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e] * (feature_dim - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e), dtype = torch.float32))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Linear(feature_dim, cap_dim), nn.GELU(),","            nn.Linear(cap_dim, cap_dim),","        )","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token = nn.Linear(cap_dim, dim)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim = cap_dim","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, physical):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(b, feature_dim) -\u0026gt; ((b, cap_dim) conditioning, (b, 1, dim) token).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        cap = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net(physical * \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.scale)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e cap, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token(cap)[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, :]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- structure_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eStructureEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(nn.Sequential):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, input_dim, dim):","        super().__init__(nn.Linear(input_dim, dim), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(dim, dim))","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003epool\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, structure, structure_mask):","        rows = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e(structure)","        mask = structure_mask[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(rows.dtype)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e (rows * mask).sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) / mask.sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e).clamp(min=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- kappa_set_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eKappaSetEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, n_probes = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e, p_drop = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.3\u003c/span\u003e, hidden = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.p_drop = p_drop","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.id_embed = nn.Embedding(n_probes, hidden)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.val_mlp = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, hidden), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(hidden, hidden))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token = nn.Linear(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e * hidden, dim)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, capability):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;capability = (probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool) -\u0026gt; (b, 1, dim).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        probes, mask = capability","        mask = mask.bool()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.training \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eand\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.p_drop \u0026gt; \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e:","            keep = torch.rand(mask.shape, device = mask.device) \u0026gt;= \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.p_drop","            keep = keep \u0026amp; mask","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# never drop every probe: fall back to the original mask for those rows\u003c/span\u003e","            empty = ~keep.any(dim = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, keepdim = \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e)","            mask = torch.where(empty, mask, keep)","        tok = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.id_embed(probes[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e].long()) + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.val_mlp(probes[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e:\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e])  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# (b, P, h)\u003c/span\u003e","        m = mask[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(tok.dtype)","        mean = (tok * m).sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) / m.sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e).clamp(min = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e)","        mx = tok.masked_fill(~mask[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e], float(\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026#x27;-inf\u0026#x27;\u003c/span\u003e)).amax(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","        mx = torch.where(torch.isfinite(mx), mx, torch.zeros_like(mx))  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# all-masked row -\u0026gt; 0\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token(torch.cat([mean, mx], dim = -\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e))[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, :]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e_self_check\u003c/span\u003e():","    torch.manual_seed(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e)","    enc = KappaSetEncoder(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e32\u003c/span\u003e, n_probes = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e, p_drop = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.3\u003c/span\u003e).eval()","    b, P = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e","    probes = torch.stack([torch.arange(P).float(), torch.rand(P), torch.rand(P).round()], -\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)[\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].repeat(b, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","    mask = torch.ones(b, P, dtype = torch.bool)","    out = enc((probes, mask))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e out.shape == (b, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e32\u003c/span\u003e), out.shape","    perm = torch.randperm(P)","    out_p = enc((probes[:, perm], mask[:, perm]))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e torch.allclose(out, out_p, atol = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-5\u003c/span\u003e), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;not permutation invariant\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# mask handling: masking probe 3 == physically removing it\u003c/span\u003e","    mask2 = mask.clone(); mask2[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e] = \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e","    keep = [i \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e i \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e range(P) \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e i != \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e]","    a = enc((probes, mask2)); c = enc((probes[:, keep], mask[:, keep]))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e torch.allclose(a, c, atol = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-5\u003c/span\u003e), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;masked probe leaks into the token\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e torch.allclose(a, out, atol = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-3\u003c/span\u003e), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;removing a probe changed nothing\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# training drop never empties a row\u003c/span\u003e","    enc.train()","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e _ \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e range(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e):","        o = enc((probes, mask))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e torch.isfinite(o).all()","    print(\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;ok KappaSetEncoder: shape (b,1,dim), permutation-invariant, mask == removal, drop finite\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)"],"formatted":{"text":"\"\"\"encoders: scene_encoder, perception_encoder, capability_encoder, structure_encoder, kappa_set_encoder.\n\nscene_encoder: Scene encoder + object tokenizer: raw scene inputs -\u003e tokens.\n\nein notation:\n  b - batch\n  n - objects\n  s - scene tokens\n  d - model dimension\n\nperception_encoder: Perception encoder: metric terrain + embodiment -\u003e per-cell features.\n\nThis is the box the grid pipeline skipped. There, `project.classify_terrain`\nthresholded heights into FLAT/STEP/WALL with two global constants and the\nnetwork saw only the one-hot result, so it could not represent \"0.29 m ledge\"\nat all, and every body shared one classification.\n\nHere the encoder consumes metres and is conditioned on the body, because\ntraversability is a joint function of the two. The conditioning is FiLM rather\nthan a concatenated token: a wheel and a humanoid looking at the same ledge\nmust produce *different features for the same pixel*, which is a per-location\nmodulation, not a global summary another layer has to route.\n\nWhat is handed over and what is learned, deliberately:\n\n  handed over   the signed step-up to each 4-neighbour (`edge_deltas`). It is\n                an exact finite difference of the input, so making a 3x3 conv\n                rediscover it only adds an approximation error right where the\n                decision boundary is.\n\n  learned       the comparison of that step-up against the body's climb limit.\n                Feeding `limit - delta` directly would make the auxiliary head\n                trivial and measure nothing; leaving it to FiLM means the head's\n                accuracy is evidence that capability conditioning works, and\n                that evidence transfers to bodies with limits never trained on.\n\nein notation:\n  b - batch      d - channels\n  h, w - grid    e - edge directions (4)\n\ncapability_encoder: LEGACY capability encoder: the spec-sheet path. Superseded by KappaSetEncoder.\n\nThis encodes capability.feature_vector -- a fixed table of limits (terrain\nclasses, mass / extent caps, arms) handed to the model as ground truth. That\nframing is retired (2026-09-02): kappa is now a MEASURED behavioral profile --\n(probe, outcome, provenance) rows produced by the calibration instruments in\nexperiments/kappa_measure/ (rendered in experiments/kappa_arena/) and encoded\nby model/kappa_set_encoder.py, which is the default in PAMO and train_clear.\n\nThis class stays only so pre-kappa checkpoints keep loading\n(capability_encoder='vector'). Do not reach for it in new work: a spec sheet\ncannot say \"untested\", cannot carry a success RATE, and cannot grow a row\nwithout a retrain -- the three properties the measured set was built for.\n\nstructure_encoder: Row MLP and masked pooling, with the original Sequential checkpoint keys.\n\nkappa_set_encoder: KappaSetEncoder: a SET of probe observations -\u003e one capability token.\n\nDrop-in for CapabilityEncoder (same (b, 1, dim) output) but the input is\n`(probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool)` from data.probes, not a fixed\nvector. Per-probe token = Embedding(probe_id) + MLP([query, outcome]);\nmasked mean + max pooling (DeepSets) -\u003e Linear. Permutation-invariant by\nconstruction, and any subset of probes is a valid input -- that is what lets a\nmeasured robot with a missing probe, or a test-time ablation of probes, reach\nthe same planner.\n\nTraining-time probe dropout: each probe dropped with p_drop, never all of them.\nEval keeps every probe the mask allows.\n\n    python -m clear.model.kappa_set_encoder   # self-check\n\"\"\"\n\n# ---- scene_encoder ----\nimport torch\nfrom einops import rearrange\nfrom torch import nn\nfrom torch.nn import Module\n\n# constants\n\nSCENE_CHANS = 5  # flat / step / wall / start / goal\nOBJ_COLS = (\"x\", \"y\", \"cos\", \"sin\", \"mass\", \"extent\", \"s\", \"t\", \"can_move\")\nOBJ_FEAT = len(OBJ_COLS)\n\n# Columns a run can withhold, to make the model work something out instead of\n# being told it.\n#\n#   'can_move'  the ANSWER to the manipulation half of the capability question.\n#   'mass'      the harder one. can_move is just mass \u003c= max_mass, both of which\n#               are handed over, so withholding only can_move leaves a\n#               comparison between two given numbers -- which is why removing it\n#               cost about one standard deviation. Withhold mass as well and the\n#               model has to read weight off the object's shape, which the\n#               generator makes possible because crate mass is density times\n#               volume.\nDROPPABLE = (\"mass\", \"can_move\")\n\n\ndef obj_feat_dim(drop=(), include_reachable=False):\n    return OBJ_FEAT - len(set(drop)) + int(include_reachable)\n\n\ndef object_features(\n    poses, mass, extent, s, t, movable, grid_hw, drop=(), reachable0=None\n):\n    \"\"\"Assemble (b, n, obj_feat_dim(drop, reachable0 is not None)) object features.\n\n    poses is (b, n, 3) = x, y, theta. `drop` names columns to withhold; see\n    DROPPABLE. `reachable0`: optional (b, n) bool -- is object i's own cell\n    reachable from scene.start with every OTHER object at its initial cell\n    (Example.reachable0, see data.py's own docstring on that field for why\n    this is missing signal, not decoration). None (default, every existing\n    call site) omits the column entirely -- byte-identical to before this\n    was added; only a model constructed with use_reachable=True passes it.\n    \"\"\"\n    h, w = grid_hw\n    scale = poses.new_tensor([w - 1, h - 1])\n    xy = poses[..., :2] / scale * 2 - 1\n    theta = poses[..., 2]\n    t = torch.as_tensor(t, dtype=poses.dtype, device=poses.device)\n    t = (t[:, None] if t.dim() == 1 else t).expand(s.shape)\n    cols = [\n        xy[..., 0],\n        xy[..., 1],\n        torch.cos(theta),\n        torch.sin(theta),\n        torch.log1p(mass) / 3.0,\n        extent,\n        s,\n        t,\n        movable.to(poses.dtype),\n    ]\n    drop = set(drop)\n    assert drop \u003c= set(DROPPABLE), f\"cannot drop {drop - set(DROPPABLE)}\"\n    feats = [c for name, c in zip(OBJ_COLS, cols) if name not in drop]\n    if reachable0 is not None:\n        feats.append(reachable0.to(poses.dtype))\n    return torch.stack(feats, dim=-1)\n\n\n# scene encoder\n\n\nclass SceneEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Terrain / occupancy grid -\u003e a small set of spatial tokens.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, grid_hw, channels=SCENE_CHANS, stride=2):\n        \"\"\"stride 2 (default): one token per 2x2 patch. stride 1: one token per CELL -- so a\n        terrain token is a single cell's ground, not a pooled patch (PriorityHead scene_stride).\n        \"\"\"\n        super().__init__()\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(channels, dim // 2, 3, padding=1),\n            nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv2d(dim // 2, dim, 3, stride=stride, padding=1),\n            nn.GELU(),\n        )\n        h, w = grid_hw\n        self.stride = stride\n        self.num_tokens = ((h + stride - 1) // stride) * ((w + stride - 1) // stride)\n        self.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, self.num_tokens, dim))\n\n    def forward(self, grid):\n        tokens = rearrange(self.net(grid), \"b d h w -\u003e b (h w) d\")\n        return tokens + self.pos_emb\n\n\ndef grow_scene_channels(\n    state_dict,\n    new_channels,\n    prefixes=(\"priority_head.scene_encoder\", \"velocity_field.scene_encoder\"),\n):\n    \"\"\"Widen a checkpoint's scene-encoder input conv from C to `new_channels`.\n\n    The extra channels are initialised to ZERO, so the grown model computes\n    EXACTLY what the original did on its first forward pass and then learns to\n    use the new inputs -- the same reason CrossTracer initialises its FiLM\n    layers near identity. A random init here would instead throw away the\n    trained representation the moment the ego channels are attached, which is\n    indistinguishable from \"the ego channels hurt\" when the run is scored.\n\n    Relies on the channel contract in `data/ego_project.py`: the five class\n    channels stay FIRST, so `w[:, :C]` keeps its meaning. Reordering them would\n    silently mis-wire every grown checkpoint.\n\n    -\u003e (state_dict, [names of the tensors that were widened]). Mutates a copy.\n    \"\"\"\n    out, grown = dict(state_dict), []\n    for pre in prefixes:\n        key = f\"{pre}.net.0.weight\"\n        if key not in out:\n            continue\n        w = out[key]\n        c = w.shape[1]\n        if c == new_channels:\n            continue\n        if c \u003e new_channels:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{key} has {c} channels, cannot shrink to {new_channels}\")\n        wide = w.new_zeros((w.shape[0], new_channels) + tuple(w.shape[2:]))\n        wide[:, :c] = w\n        out[key] = wide\n        grown.append(key)\n    return out, grown\n\n\nclass MetricSceneEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Perception features -\u003e spatial tokens, for the metric-terrain path.\n\n    SceneEncoder above takes the 5-channel class grid and is what the grid\n    experiments train on. This one takes what PerceptionEncoder produced --\n    per-cell features that already know the height field AND the body looking\n    at it -- and only does the pooling into tokens.\n\n    Keeping the two separate rather than adding a flag: they consume different\n    worlds, and a shared class whose first line branches on which is a merge\n    conflict waiting for the day the class grid is deleted.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, grid_hw, in_dim):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.proj = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(in_dim, dim, 3, stride=2, padding=1),\n            nn.GELU(),\n        )\n        h, w = grid_hw\n        self.num_tokens = ((h + 1) // 2) * ((w + 1) // 2)\n        self.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, self.num_tokens, dim))\n\n    def forward(self, features):\n        tokens = rearrange(self.proj(features), \"b d h w -\u003e b (h w) d\")\n        return tokens + self.pos_emb\n\n\n# ---- perception_encoder ----\nfrom clear.data.terrain import EDGES, OFF_GRID_STEP\n\n# input channel budget: height, 4 edge deltas, occupancy, start, goal\nPERCEPT_CHANS = 1 + len(EDGES) + 3\n\n# metres; real terrain tops out at 1.0 m (mj_maze wall slabs). Off-grid edges\n# arrive as a large sentinel -- clamping keeps them distinctly \"unclimbable\"\n# without letting one channel dominate the input scale.\nHEIGHT_CLAMP = 1.5\n\n\ndef edge_deltas_torch(heights):\n    \"\"\"(b, h, w) metric heights -\u003e (b, 4, h, w) signed step-up per neighbour.\n\n    Mirrors data.terrain.edge_deltas exactly (same EDGES order, same off-grid\n    sentinel) so labels and inputs cannot drift apart; tests/test_perception.py\n    asserts they agree elementwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    b, h, w = heights.shape\n    out = heights.new_empty((b, len(EDGES), h, w))\n    for k, (dr, dc) in enumerate(EDGES):\n        nb = heights.new_full((b, h, w), OFF_GRID_STEP)\n        r0, r1 = max(0, -dr), h - max(0, dr)\n        c0, c1 = max(0, -dc), w - max(0, dc)\n        nb[:, r0:r1, c0:c1] = heights[:, r0 + dr : r1 + dr, c0 + dc : c1 + dc]\n        out[:, k] = nb - heights\n    return out\n\n\ndef perception_input(heights, occupancy, start, goal):\n    \"\"\"Assemble (b, PERCEPT_CHANS, h, w). All inputs are (b, h, w).\"\"\"\n    deltas = edge_deltas_torch(heights).clamp(-HEIGHT_CLAMP, HEIGHT_CLAMP)\n    return torch.cat(\n        [\n            (heights / HEIGHT_CLAMP)[:, None],\n            deltas / HEIGHT_CLAMP,\n            occupancy[:, None].to(heights.dtype),\n            start[:, None].to(heights.dtype),\n            goal[:, None].to(heights.dtype),\n        ],\n        dim=1,\n    )\n\n\nclass FiLM(Module):\n    \"\"\"Per-channel affine modulation from the capability vector.\n\n    Zero-initialised so the encoder starts as the unconditioned network and\n    conditioning is something it acquires -- the same reason the AdaLN blocks\n    in the dynamics flow start at identity. A randomly initialised FiLM\n    multiplies early features by noise that depends on the body, which reads\n    to the optimiser as label noise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, cap_dim, channels):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.to_scale_shift = nn.Linear(cap_dim, channels * 2)\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.to_scale_shift.weight)\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.to_scale_shift.bias)\n\n    def forward(self, x, cap):\n        scale, shift = self.to_scale_shift(cap).chunk(2, dim=-1)\n        return x * (1.0 + scale[..., None, None]) + shift[..., None, None]\n\n\nclass PerceptionEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"(heights, occupancy, start, goal, capability) -\u003e (b, dim, h, w) features\n    plus per-edge traversability logits.\n\n    The auxiliary head is not decoration. Scene success is a single number at\n    the end of a long pipeline; per-edge traversability is dense, exactly\n    supervised, and fails loudly the moment capability conditioning stops\n    working. Train with it, read it, and only then trust the rest.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, cap_dim, depth=3, in_chans=PERCEPT_CHANS, cond=\"film\"):\n        super().__init__()\n        assert cond in (\"film\", \"concat\"), cond\n        # 'concat' is the ablation: the same capability vector broadcast as\n        # constant input channels, i.e. told once at the input instead of at\n        # every layer and location. Keeping it here rather than in a fork means\n        # the two share every other line, so a difference is the conditioning.\n        self.cond = cond\n        self.cap_dim = cap_dim\n        self.stem = nn.Conv2d(\n            in_chans + (cap_dim if cond == \"concat\" else 0), dim, 3, padding=1\n        )\n        self.blocks = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.films = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.norms = nn.ModuleList()\n        for _ in range(depth):\n            self.blocks.append(nn.Conv2d(dim, dim, 3, padding=1))\n            self.norms.append(nn.GroupNorm(min(8, dim), dim))\n            self.films.append(FiLM(cap_dim, dim))\n        self.act = nn.GELU()\n        self.stem_film = FiLM(cap_dim, dim)\n        self.edge_head = nn.Conv2d(dim, len(EDGES), 1)\n\n    def forward(self, heights, occupancy, start, goal, cap):\n        inp = perception_input(heights, occupancy, start, goal)\n        if self.cond == \"concat\":\n            b, _, h, w = inp.shape\n            inp = torch.cat(\n                [inp, cap[:, :, None, None].expand(b, self.cap_dim, h, w)], 1\n            )\n            x = self.act(self.stem(inp))\n            for conv, norm in zip(self.blocks, self.norms):\n                x = x + self.act(norm(conv(x)))\n        else:\n            x = self.act(self.stem_film(self.stem(inp), cap))\n            for conv, norm, film in zip(self.blocks, self.norms, self.films):\n                x = x + self.act(film(norm(conv(x)), cap))\n        return x, self.edge_head(x)\n\n\n# ---- capability_encoder ----\nfrom clear.data.capability import FEATURE_DIM, PHYSICAL_DIM\n\n\nclass CapabilityEncoder(Module):\n    def __init__(self, dim, feature_dim=FEATURE_DIM):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.to_token = nn.Linear(feature_dim, dim)\n\n    def forward(self, capability):\n        \"\"\"(b, feature_dim) -\u003e (b, 1, d) embodiment token.\"\"\"\n        return self.to_token(capability)[:, None, :]\n\n\nclass SensitivityHead(Module):\n    \"\"\"Hard-example reweighting for physical-cost loss terms -- iteration 2,\n    superseding the CrossTracer-style learned-per-embodiment-MLP version\n    (arXiv 2601's \"Embodiment Sensitivity Head\" -- see\n    docs/RESEARCH_coins_crosstracer_ordering.md for the full history).\n\n    Read by PAMO.forward() (learned_loss_weight=True) to replace the single\n    hand-tuned endpoint_weight/validity_weight constant, shared across every\n    example, with a per-object multiplier -- see clear.py's own comment on\n    those constants pulling in opposite directions for discrete vs\n    continuous.\n\n    **Why this isn't `alpha_e = f(emb_feat)` any more.** Two iterations of\n    that design (unbounded Softplus, then bounded-via-tanh to [0.5, 1.5])\n    both collapsed to the SAME degenerate pattern in every seed tested: two\n    of the three embodiments pinned at the minimum weight, one at the\n    maximum. Root cause, confirmed by measuring per-embodiment endpoint\n    error directly on an unbiased checkpoint (`runs/llw_ablation/\n    llw_base_seed0`): wheel=0.0501, quadruped=0.0173, humanoid=0.0042 --\n    the head was upweighting whichever embodiment ALREADY had the LOWEST\n    error, not the highest. This is not a tuning problem, it's structural:\n    for a normalized weighted mean `L = sum(alpha_i * err_i) / sum(alpha_i)`,\n    `dL/d(alpha_i) ~ (err_i - L)`, so gradient descent on `alpha` (however\n    it's parameterized, learned from emb_feat or anything else) always\n    increases weight on below-average-error terms and decreases it on\n    above-average ones -- exactly backwards from \"pay more attention to\n    what's hard\", regardless of how tightly alpha is bounded.\n\n    **This version has no learned parameters at all**, precisely because a\n    learned function of anything, trained end-to-end against this same\n    normalized loss, inherits the same backwards incentive. Instead, alpha\n    is a direct, monotonically INCREASING function of each object's own\n    CURRENT error, ALREADY-DETACHED by the caller before it reaches here --\n    the classic hard-example-reweighting / OHEM / focal-loss recipe. With\n    no free parameters, there is nothing left for gradient descent to game.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    MAX_DEV = 0.5  # alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV] -- same bound as the superseded\n    # learned version, kept for comparability; not itself what fixes the incentive here.\n\n    def forward(self, err, movable):\n        \"\"\"err: (b, n) per-object error the caller has ALREADY detached (this\n        function never calls .detach() itself -- the caller decides what\n        \"error\" means, endpoint error today). movable: (b, n) bool.\n        -\u003e (b, n) alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV], centered on the\n        batch's own mean movable-object error (an average-error object gets\n        alpha == 1.0; above-average gets \u003e 1.0; below-average gets \u003c 1.0).\"\"\"\n        mv = movable.to(err.dtype)\n        n = mv.sum().clamp(min=1.0)\n        mean = (err * mv).sum() / n\n        var = (((err - mean) ** 2) * mv).sum() / n\n        std = var.clamp(min=1e-8).sqrt()\n        z = (err - mean) / std\n        return 1.0 + self.MAX_DEV * torch.tanh(z)\n\n\nclass MorphCapabilityEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Link rows -\u003e (conditioning vector, token): kappa = e(morphology) for the\n    metric front end (docs/PREREGISTRATION_learned_ccor_2026-09-02.md follow-up).\n\n    Same output contract as PhysicalCapabilityEncoder -- a cap_dim vector that\n    FiLMs perception and a (b, 1, dim) token for the transformer -- but the\n    input is (morph_rows, morph_mask) from data/morphology.py, so the body's\n    STRUCTURE is the only capability channel; no limit is ever handed over.\n    The token comes from the adopted v1 set-attention MorphologyEncoder\n    (EXPERIMENT_morph_kappa_2026-09-02.md); the conditioning vector is a linear\n    read of that token.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, cap_dim=64, hidden=128, depth=2, heads=4, p_drop=0.15):\n        super().__init__()\n        from clear.model.morphology_encoder import MorphologyEncoder\n\n        self.enc = MorphologyEncoder(\n            dim, hidden=hidden, depth=depth, heads=heads, p_drop=p_drop\n        )\n        self.to_cap = nn.Linear(dim, cap_dim)\n        self.cap_dim = cap_dim\n\n    def forward(self, capability):\n        \"\"\"((b, L, F) rows, (b, L) mask) -\u003e ((b, cap_dim), (b, 1, dim)).\"\"\"\n        tok = self.enc(capability)\n        return self.to_cap(tok[:, 0]), tok\n\n\nclass PhysicalCapabilityEncoder(Module):\n    \"\"\"Metric descriptor -\u003e (conditioning vector, token).\n\n    Separate from CapabilityEncoder above because it answers a different\n    question. That one summarises a body for the ordering transformer, where a\n    single token attended over is enough. This one drives FiLM inside the\n    perception encoder, where the body has to change how a *pixel* is read --\n    so it produces a vector consumed at every spatial location, and a token for\n    the transformer as a by-product.\n\n    The input is capability.physical_vector: metres and kilograms, no class\n    membership. That is what makes an unseen climb limit a valid input rather\n    than an out-of-vocabulary one.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, dim, cap_dim=64, feature_dim=PHYSICAL_DIM):\n        super().__init__()\n        # climb is in metres and everything else is already O(1); normalise the\n        # first channel here rather than at every call site.\n        self.register_buffer(\n            \"scale\",\n            torch.tensor(\n                [1.0 / HEIGHT_CLAMP] + [1.0] * (feature_dim - 1), dtype=torch.float32\n            ),\n        )\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(feature_dim, cap_dim),\n            nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Linear(cap_dim, cap_dim),\n        )\n        self.to_token = nn.Linear(cap_dim, dim)\n        self.cap_dim = cap_dim\n\n    def forward(self, physical):\n        \"\"\"(b, feature_dim) -\u003e ((b, cap_dim) conditioning, (b, 1, dim) token).\"\"\"\n        cap = self.net(physical * self.scale)\n        return cap, self.to_token(cap)[:, None, :]\n\n\n# ---- structure_encoder ----\nclass StructureEncoder(nn.Sequential):\n    def __init__(self, input_dim, dim):\n        super().__init__(nn.Linear(input_dim, dim), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(dim, dim))\n\n    def pool(self, structure, structure_mask):\n        rows = self(structure)\n        mask = structure_mask[..., None].to(rows.dtype)\n        return (rows * mask).sum(1) / mask.sum(1).clamp(min=1)\n\n\n# ---- kappa_set_encoder ----\nclass KappaSetEncoder(Module):\n    def __init__(self, dim, n_probes=10, p_drop=0.3, hidden=64):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.p_drop = p_drop\n        self.id_embed = nn.Embedding(n_probes, hidden)\n        self.val_mlp = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(2, hidden), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(hidden, hidden)\n        )\n        self.to_token = nn.Linear(2 * hidden, dim)\n\n    def forward(self, capability):\n        \"\"\"capability = (probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool) -\u003e (b, 1, dim).\"\"\"\n        probes, mask = capability\n        mask = mask.bool()\n        if self.training and self.p_drop \u003e 0:\n            keep = torch.rand(mask.shape, device=mask.device) \u003e= self.p_drop\n            keep = keep \u0026 mask\n            # never drop every probe: fall back to the original mask for those rows\n            empty = ~keep.any(dim=1, keepdim=True)\n            mask = torch.where(empty, mask, keep)\n        tok = self.id_embed(probes[..., 0].long()) + self.val_mlp(\n            probes[..., 1:3]\n        )  # (b, P, h)\n        m = mask[..., None].to(tok.dtype)\n        mean = (tok * m).sum(1) / m.sum(1).clamp(min=1.0)\n        mx = tok.masked_fill(~mask[..., None], float(\"-inf\")).amax(1)\n        mx = torch.where(\n            torch.isfinite(mx), mx, torch.zeros_like(mx)\n        )  # all-masked row -\u003e 0\n        return self.to_token(torch.cat([mean, mx], dim=-1))[:, None, :]\n\n\ndef _self_check():\n    torch.manual_seed(0)\n    enc = KappaSetEncoder(32, n_probes=10, p_drop=0.3).eval()\n    b, P = 4, 10\n    probes = torch.stack(\n        [torch.arange(P).float(), torch.rand(P), torch.rand(P).round()], -1\n    )[None].repeat(b, 1, 1)\n    mask = torch.ones(b, P, dtype=torch.bool)\n    out = enc((probes, mask))\n    assert out.shape == (b, 1, 32), out.shape\n    perm = torch.randperm(P)\n    out_p = enc((probes[:, perm], mask[:, perm]))\n    assert torch.allclose(out, out_p, atol=1e-5), \"not permutation invariant\"\n    # mask handling: masking probe 3 == physically removing it\n    mask2 = mask.clone()\n    mask2[:, 3] = False\n    keep = [i for i in range(P) if i != 3]\n    a = enc((probes, mask2))\n    c = enc((probes[:, keep], mask[:, keep]))\n    assert torch.allclose(a, c, atol=1e-5), \"masked probe leaks into the token\"\n    assert not torch.allclose(a, out, atol=1e-3), \"removing a probe changed nothing\"\n    # training drop never empties a row\n    enc.train()\n    for _ in range(20):\n        o = enc((probes, mask))\n        assert torch.isfinite(o).all()\n    print(\n        \"ok KappaSetEncoder: shape (b,1,dim), permutation-invariant, mask == removal, drop finite\"\n    )\n","lines":["\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;encoders: scene_encoder, perception_encoder, capability_encoder, structure_encoder, kappa_set_encoder.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003escene_encoder: Scene encoder + object tokenizer: raw scene inputs -\u0026gt; tokens.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eein notation:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  b - batch\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  n - objects\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  s - scene tokens\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  d - model dimension\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eperception_encoder: Perception encoder: metric terrain + embodiment -\u0026gt; per-cell features.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eThis is the box the grid pipeline skipped. There, `project.classify_terrain`\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ethresholded heights into FLAT/STEP/WALL with two global constants and the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003enetwork saw only the one-hot result, so it could not represent \u0026quot;0.29 m ledge\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eat all, and every body shared one classification.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eHere the encoder consumes metres and is conditioned on the body, because\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003etraversability is a joint function of the two. The conditioning is FiLM rather\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ethan a concatenated token: a wheel and a humanoid looking at the same ledge\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emust produce *different features for the same pixel*, which is a per-location\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emodulation, not a global summary another layer has to route.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eWhat is handed over and what is learned, deliberately:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  handed over   the signed step-up to each 4-neighbour (`edge_deltas`). It is\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                an exact finite difference of the input, so making a 3x3 conv\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                rediscover it only adds an approximation error right where the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                decision boundary is.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  learned       the comparison of that step-up against the body\u0026#x27;s climb limit.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                Feeding `limit - delta` directly would make the auxiliary head\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                trivial and measure nothing; leaving it to FiLM means the head\u0026#x27;s\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                accuracy is evidence that capability conditioning works, and\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e                that evidence transfers to bodies with limits never trained on.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eein notation:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  b - batch      d - channels\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e  h, w - grid    e - edge directions (4)\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ecapability_encoder: LEGACY capability encoder: the spec-sheet path. Superseded by KappaSetEncoder.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eThis encodes capability.feature_vector -- a fixed table of limits (terrain\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eclasses, mass / extent caps, arms) handed to the model as ground truth. That\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eframing is retired (2026-09-02): kappa is now a MEASURED behavioral profile --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e(probe, outcome, provenance) rows produced by the calibration instruments in\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eexperiments/kappa_measure/ (rendered in experiments/kappa_arena/) and encoded\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eby model/kappa_set_encoder.py, which is the default in PAMO and train_clear.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eThis class stays only so pre-kappa checkpoints keep loading\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e(capability_encoder=\u0026#x27;vector\u0026#x27;). Do not reach for it in new work: a spec sheet\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ecannot say \u0026quot;untested\u0026quot;, cannot carry a success RATE, and cannot grow a row\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ewithout a retrain -- the three properties the measured set was built for.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003estructure_encoder: Row MLP and masked pooling, with the original Sequential checkpoint keys.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ekappa_set_encoder: KappaSetEncoder: a SET of probe observations -\u0026gt; one capability token.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eDrop-in for CapabilityEncoder (same (b, 1, dim) output) but the input is\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e`(probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool)` from data.probes, not a fixed\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003evector. Per-probe token = Embedding(probe_id) + MLP([query, outcome]);\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emasked mean + max pooling (DeepSets) -\u0026gt; Linear. Permutation-invariant by\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003econstruction, and any subset of probes is a valid input -- that is what lets a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003emeasured robot with a missing probe, or a test-time ablation of probes, reach\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003ethe same planner.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eTraining-time probe dropout: each probe dropped with p_drop, never all of them.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003eEval keeps every probe the mask allows.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    python -m clear.model.kappa_set_encoder   # self-check\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- scene_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e torch","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e einops \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e rearrange","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e torch \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e nn","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e torch.nn \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e Module","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# constants\u003c/span\u003e","","SCENE_CHANS = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e5\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# flat / step / wall / start / goal\u003c/span\u003e","OBJ_COLS = (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;x\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;y\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;cos\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;sin\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;mass\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;extent\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;s\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;t\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;can_move\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)","OBJ_FEAT = len(OBJ_COLS)","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# Columns a run can withhold, to make the model work something out instead of\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# being told it.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#   \u0026#x27;can_move\u0026#x27;  the ANSWER to the manipulation half of the capability question.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#   \u0026#x27;mass\u0026#x27;      the harder one. can_move is just mass \u0026lt;= max_mass, both of which\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               are handed over, so withholding only can_move leaves a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               comparison between two given numbers -- which is why removing it\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               cost about one standard deviation. Withhold mass as well and the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               model has to read weight off the object\u0026#x27;s shape, which the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               generator makes possible because crate mass is density times\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e#               volume.\u003c/span\u003e","DROPPABLE = (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;mass\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;can_move\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eobj_feat_dim\u003c/span\u003e(drop=(), include_reachable=\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e OBJ_FEAT - len(set(drop)) + int(include_reachable)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eobject_features\u003c/span\u003e(","    poses, mass, extent, s, t, movable, grid_hw, drop=(), reachable0=\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e","):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Assemble (b, n, obj_feat_dim(drop, reachable0 is not None)) object features.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    poses is (b, n, 3) = x, y, theta. `drop` names columns to withhold; see\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    DROPPABLE. `reachable0`: optional (b, n) bool -- is object i\u0026#x27;s own cell\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    reachable from scene.start with every OTHER object at its initial cell\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    (Example.reachable0, see data.py\u0026#x27;s own docstring on that field for why\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    this is missing signal, not decoration). None (default, every existing\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    call site) omits the column entirely -- byte-identical to before this\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    was added; only a model constructed with use_reachable=True passes it.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    h, w = grid_hw","    scale = poses.new_tensor([w - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, h - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e])","    xy = poses[..., :\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e] / scale * \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e","    theta = poses[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e]","    t = torch.as_tensor(t, dtype=poses.dtype, device=poses.device)","    t = (t[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e] \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e t.dim() == \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e t).expand(s.shape)","    cols = [","        xy[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e],","        xy[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e],","        torch.cos(theta),","        torch.sin(theta),","        torch.log1p(mass) / \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3.0\u003c/span\u003e,","        extent,","        s,","        t,","        movable.to(poses.dtype),","    ]","    drop = set(drop)","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e drop \u0026lt;= set(DROPPABLE), f\u0026quot;cannot drop {drop - set(DROPPABLE)}\u0026quot;","    feats = [c \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e name, c \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e zip(OBJ_COLS, cols) \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e name \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e drop]","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e reachable0 \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e:","        feats.append(reachable0.to(poses.dtype))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e torch.stack(feats, dim=-\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# scene encoder\u003c/span\u003e","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eSceneEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Terrain / occupancy grid -\u0026gt; a small set of spatial tokens.\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, grid_hw, channels=SCENE_CHANS, stride=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;stride 2 (default): one token per 2x2 patch. stride 1: one token per CELL -- so a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        terrain token is a single cell\u0026#x27;s ground, not a pooled patch (PriorityHead scene_stride).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Conv2d(channels, dim // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, padding=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e),","            nn.GELU(),","            nn.Conv2d(dim // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, stride=stride, padding=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e),","            nn.GELU(),","        )","        h, w = grid_hw","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stride = stride","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens = ((h + stride - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // stride) * ((w + stride - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // stride)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens, dim))","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, grid):","        tokens = rearrange(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net(grid), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;b d h w -\u0026gt; b (h w) d\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e tokens + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003egrow_scene_channels\u003c/span\u003e(","    state_dict,","    new_channels,","    prefixes=(\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;priority_head.scene_encoder\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;velocity_field.scene_encoder\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e),","):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Widen a checkpoint\u0026#x27;s scene-encoder input conv from C to `new_channels`.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The extra channels are initialised to ZERO, so the grown model computes\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    EXACTLY what the original did on its first forward pass and then learns to\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    use the new inputs -- the same reason CrossTracer initialises its FiLM\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    layers near identity. A random init here would instead throw away the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    trained representation the moment the ego channels are attached, which is\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    indistinguishable from \u0026quot;the ego channels hurt\u0026quot; when the run is scored.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Relies on the channel contract in `data/ego_project.py`: the five class\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    channels stay FIRST, so `w[:, :C]` keeps its meaning. Reordering them would\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    silently mis-wire every grown checkpoint.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    -\u0026gt; (state_dict, [names of the tensors that were widened]). Mutates a copy.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    out, grown = dict(state_dict), []","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e pre \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e prefixes:","        key = f\u0026quot;{pre}.net.0.weight\u0026quot;","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e key \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e out:","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003econtinue\u003c/span\u003e","        w = out[key]","        c = w.shape[\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e]","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e c == new_channels:","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003econtinue\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e c \u0026gt; new_channels:","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eraise\u003c/span\u003e ValueError(f\u0026quot;{key} has {c} channels, cannot shrink to {new_channels}\u0026quot;)","        wide = w.new_zeros((w.shape[\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e], new_channels) + tuple(w.shape[\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e:]))","        wide[:, :c] = w","        out[key] = wide","        grown.append(key)","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e out, grown","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eMetricSceneEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Perception features -\u0026gt; spatial tokens, for the metric-terrain path.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    SceneEncoder above takes the 5-channel class grid and is what the grid\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    experiments train on. This one takes what PerceptionEncoder produced --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    per-cell features that already know the height field AND the body looking\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    at it -- and only does the pooling into tokens.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Keeping the two separate rather than adding a flag: they consume different\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    worlds, and a shared class whose first line branches on which is a merge\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    conflict waiting for the day the class grid is deleted.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, grid_hw, in_dim):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.proj = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Conv2d(in_dim, dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, stride=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, padding=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e),","            nn.GELU(),","        )","        h, w = grid_hw","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens = ((h + \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e) * ((w + \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) // \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.num_tokens, dim))","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, features):","        tokens = rearrange(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.proj(features), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;b d h w -\u0026gt; b (h w) d\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e tokens + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.pos_emb","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- perception_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e clear.data.terrain \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e EDGES, OFF_GRID_STEP","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# input channel budget: height, 4 edge deltas, occupancy, start, goal\u003c/span\u003e","PERCEPT_CHANS = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e + len(EDGES) + \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# metres; real terrain tops out at 1.0 m (mj_maze wall slabs). Off-grid edges\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# arrive as a large sentinel -- clamping keeps them distinctly \u0026quot;unclimbable\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# without letting one channel dominate the input scale.\u003c/span\u003e","HEIGHT_CLAMP = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.5\u003c/span\u003e","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eedge_deltas_torch\u003c/span\u003e(heights):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(b, h, w) metric heights -\u0026gt; (b, 4, h, w) signed step-up per neighbour.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Mirrors data.terrain.edge_deltas exactly (same EDGES order, same off-grid\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    sentinel) so labels and inputs cannot drift apart; tests/test_perception.py\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    asserts they agree elementwise.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    b, h, w = heights.shape","    out = heights.new_empty((b, len(EDGES), h, w))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e k, (dr, dc) \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e enumerate(EDGES):","        nb = heights.new_full((b, h, w), OFF_GRID_STEP)","        r0, r1 = max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, -dr), h - max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, dr)","        c0, c1 = max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, -dc), w - max(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e, dc)","        nb[:, r0:r1, c0:c1] = heights[:, r0 + dr : r1 + dr, c0 + dc : c1 + dc]","        out[:, k] = nb - heights","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e out","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eperception_input\u003c/span\u003e(heights, occupancy, start, goal):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Assemble (b, PERCEPT_CHANS, h, w). All inputs are (b, h, w).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    deltas = edge_deltas_torch(heights).clamp(-HEIGHT_CLAMP, HEIGHT_CLAMP)","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e torch.cat(","        [","            (heights / HEIGHT_CLAMP)[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e],","            deltas / HEIGHT_CLAMP,","            occupancy[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(heights.dtype),","            start[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(heights.dtype),","            goal[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(heights.dtype),","        ],","        dim=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e,","    )","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eFiLM\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Per-channel affine modulation from the capability vector.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Zero-initialised so the encoder starts as the unconditioned network and\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    conditioning is something it acquires -- the same reason the AdaLN blocks\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    in the dynamics flow start at identity. A randomly initialised FiLM\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    multiplies early features by noise that depends on the body, which reads\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    to the optimiser as label noise.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, cap_dim, channels):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift = nn.Linear(cap_dim, channels * \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e)","        nn.init.zeros_(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift.weight)","        nn.init.zeros_(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift.bias)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, x, cap):","        scale, shift = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_scale_shift(cap).chunk(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, dim=-\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e x * (\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e + scale[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e]) + shift[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003ePerceptionEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(heights, occupancy, start, goal, capability) -\u0026gt; (b, dim, h, w) features\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    plus per-edge traversability logits.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The auxiliary head is not decoration. Scene success is a single number at\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the end of a long pipeline; per-edge traversability is dense, exactly\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    supervised, and fails loudly the moment capability conditioning stops\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    working. Train with it, read it, and only then trust the rest.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, cap_dim, depth=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, in_chans=PERCEPT_CHANS, cond=\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;film\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e cond \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e (\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;film\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;concat\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e), cond","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# \u0026#x27;concat\u0026#x27; is the ablation: the same capability vector broadcast as\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# constant input channels, i.e. told once at the input instead of at\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# every layer and location. Keeping it here rather than in a fork means\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# the two share every other line, so a difference is the conditioning.\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cond = cond","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim = cap_dim","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem = nn.Conv2d(","            in_chans + (cap_dim \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e cond == \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;concat\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e), dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, padding=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e","        )","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks = nn.ModuleList()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.films = nn.ModuleList()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms = nn.ModuleList()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e _ \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e range(depth):","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks.append(nn.Conv2d(dim, dim, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e, padding=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms.append(nn.GroupNorm(min(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e8\u003c/span\u003e, dim), dim))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.films.append(FiLM(cap_dim, dim))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act = nn.GELU()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem_film = FiLM(cap_dim, dim)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.edge_head = nn.Conv2d(dim, len(EDGES), \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, heights, occupancy, start, goal, cap):","        inp = perception_input(heights, occupancy, start, goal)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cond == \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;concat\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e:","            b, _, h, w = inp.shape","            inp = torch.cat(","                [inp, cap[:, :, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].expand(b, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim, h, w)], \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e","            )","            x = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem(inp))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e conv, norm \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e zip(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms):","                x = x + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(norm(conv(x)))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e:","            x = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem_film(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.stem(inp), cap))","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e conv, norm, film \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e zip(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.blocks, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.norms, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.films):","                x = x + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.act(film(norm(conv(x)), cap))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e x, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.edge_head(x)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- capability_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e clear.data.capability \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e FEATURE_DIM, PHYSICAL_DIM","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eCapabilityEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, feature_dim=FEATURE_DIM):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token = nn.Linear(feature_dim, dim)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, capability):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(b, feature_dim) -\u0026gt; (b, 1, d) embodiment token.\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token(capability)[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, :]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eSensitivityHead\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Hard-example reweighting for physical-cost loss terms -- iteration 2,\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    superseding the CrossTracer-style learned-per-embodiment-MLP version\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    (arXiv 2601\u0026#x27;s \u0026quot;Embodiment Sensitivity Head\u0026quot; -- see\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    docs/RESEARCH_coins_crosstracer_ordering.md for the full history).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Read by PAMO.forward() (learned_loss_weight=True) to replace the single\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    hand-tuned endpoint_weight/validity_weight constant, shared across every\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    example, with a per-object multiplier -- see clear.py\u0026#x27;s own comment on\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    those constants pulling in opposite directions for discrete vs\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    continuous.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    **Why this isn\u0026#x27;t `alpha_e = f(emb_feat)` any more.** Two iterations of\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    that design (unbounded Softplus, then bounded-via-tanh to [0.5, 1.5])\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    both collapsed to the SAME degenerate pattern in every seed tested: two\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    of the three embodiments pinned at the minimum weight, one at the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    maximum. Root cause, confirmed by measuring per-embodiment endpoint\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    error directly on an unbiased checkpoint (`runs/llw_ablation/\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    llw_base_seed0`): wheel=0.0501, quadruped=0.0173, humanoid=0.0042 --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the head was upweighting whichever embodiment ALREADY had the LOWEST\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    error, not the highest. This is not a tuning problem, it\u0026#x27;s structural:\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    for a normalized weighted mean `L = sum(alpha_i * err_i) / sum(alpha_i)`,\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    `dL/d(alpha_i) ~ (err_i - L)`, so gradient descent on `alpha` (however\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    it\u0026#x27;s parameterized, learned from emb_feat or anything else) always\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    increases weight on below-average-error terms and decreases it on\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    above-average ones -- exactly backwards from \u0026quot;pay more attention to\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    what\u0026#x27;s hard\u0026quot;, regardless of how tightly alpha is bounded.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    **This version has no learned parameters at all**, precisely because a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    learned function of anything, trained end-to-end against this same\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    normalized loss, inherits the same backwards incentive. Instead, alpha\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    is a direct, monotonically INCREASING function of each object\u0026#x27;s own\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    CURRENT error, ALREADY-DETACHED by the caller before it reaches here --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the classic hard-example-reweighting / OHEM / focal-loss recipe. With\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    no free parameters, there is nothing left for gradient descent to game.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    MAX_DEV = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.5\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV] -- same bound as the superseded\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# learned version, kept for comparability; not itself what fixes the incentive here.\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, err, movable):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;err: (b, n) per-object error the caller has ALREADY detached (this\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        function never calls .detach() itself -- the caller decides what\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        \u0026quot;error\u0026quot; means, endpoint error today). movable: (b, n) bool.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        -\u0026gt; (b, n) alpha in [1 - MAX_DEV, 1 + MAX_DEV], centered on the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        batch\u0026#x27;s own mean movable-object error (an average-error object gets\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e        alpha == 1.0; above-average gets \u0026gt; 1.0; below-average gets \u0026lt; 1.0).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        mv = movable.to(err.dtype)","        n = mv.sum().clamp(min=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e)","        mean = (err * mv).sum() / n","        var = (((err - mean) ** \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e) * mv).sum() / n","        std = var.clamp(min=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-8\u003c/span\u003e).sqrt()","        z = (err - mean) / std","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.MAX_DEV * torch.tanh(z)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eMorphCapabilityEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Link rows -\u0026gt; (conditioning vector, token): kappa = e(morphology) for the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    metric front end (docs/PREREGISTRATION_learned_ccor_2026-09-02.md follow-up).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Same output contract as PhysicalCapabilityEncoder -- a cap_dim vector that\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    FiLMs perception and a (b, 1, dim) token for the transformer -- but the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    input is (morph_rows, morph_mask) from data/morphology.py, so the body\u0026#x27;s\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    STRUCTURE is the only capability channel; no limit is ever handed over.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The token comes from the adopted v1 set-attention MorphologyEncoder\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    (EXPERIMENT_morph_kappa_2026-09-02.md); the conditioning vector is a linear\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    read of that token.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, cap_dim=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e, hidden=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e128\u003c/span\u003e, depth=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, heads=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e, p_drop=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.15\u003c/span\u003e):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e clear.model.morphology_encoder \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e MorphologyEncoder","","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.enc = MorphologyEncoder(","            dim, hidden=hidden, depth=depth, heads=heads, p_drop=p_drop","        )","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_cap = nn.Linear(dim, cap_dim)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim = cap_dim","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, capability):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;((b, L, F) rows, (b, L) mask) -\u0026gt; ((b, cap_dim), (b, 1, dim)).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        tok = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.enc(capability)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_cap(tok[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e]), tok","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003ePhysicalCapabilityEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;Metric descriptor -\u0026gt; (conditioning vector, token).\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    Separate from CapabilityEncoder above because it answers a different\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    question. That one summarises a body for the ordering transformer, where a\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    single token attended over is enough. This one drives FiLM inside the\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    perception encoder, where the body has to change how a *pixel* is read --\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    so it produces a vector consumed at every spatial location, and a token for\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    the transformer as a by-product.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    The input is capability.physical_vector: metres and kilograms, no class\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    membership. That is what makes an unseen climb limit a valid input rather\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    than an out-of-vocabulary one.\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e    \u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, cap_dim=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e, feature_dim=PHYSICAL_DIM):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# climb is in metres and everything else is already O(1); normalise the\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# first channel here rather than at every call site.\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.register_buffer(","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;scale\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e,","            torch.tensor(","                [\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e / HEIGHT_CLAMP] + [\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e] * (feature_dim - \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e), dtype=torch.float32","            ),","        )","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Linear(feature_dim, cap_dim),","            nn.GELU(),","            nn.Linear(cap_dim, cap_dim),","        )","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token = nn.Linear(cap_dim, dim)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.cap_dim = cap_dim","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, physical):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;(b, feature_dim) -\u0026gt; ((b, cap_dim) conditioning, (b, 1, dim) token).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        cap = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.net(physical * \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.scale)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e cap, \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token(cap)[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, :]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- structure_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eStructureEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(nn.Sequential):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, input_dim, dim):","        super().__init__(nn.Linear(input_dim, dim), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(dim, dim))","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003epool\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, structure, structure_mask):","        rows = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e(structure)","        mask = structure_mask[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(rows.dtype)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e (rows * mask).sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) / mask.sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e).clamp(min=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# ---- kappa_set_encoder ----\u003c/span\u003e","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eKappaSetEncoder\u003c/span\u003e(Module):","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e__init__\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, dim, n_probes=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e, p_drop=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.3\u003c/span\u003e, hidden=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e64\u003c/span\u003e):","        super().__init__()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.p_drop = p_drop","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.id_embed = nn.Embedding(n_probes, hidden)","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.val_mlp = nn.Sequential(","            nn.Linear(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e, hidden), nn.GELU(), nn.Linear(hidden, hidden)","        )","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token = nn.Linear(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e * hidden, dim)","","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003eforward\u003c/span\u003e(\u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e, capability):","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;capability = (probe_set (b, P, 3), probe_mask (b, P) bool) -\u0026gt; (b, 1, dim).\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","        probes, mask = capability","        mask = mask.bool()","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.training \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eand\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.p_drop \u0026gt; \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e:","            keep = torch.rand(mask.shape, device=mask.device) \u0026gt;= \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.p_drop","            keep = keep \u0026amp; mask","            \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# never drop every probe: fall back to the original mask for those rows\u003c/span\u003e","            empty = ~keep.any(dim=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, keepdim=\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e)","            mask = torch.where(empty, mask, keep)","        tok = \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.id_embed(probes[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e].long()) + \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.val_mlp(","            probes[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e:\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e]","        )  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# (b, P, h)\u003c/span\u003e","        m = mask[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].to(tok.dtype)","        mean = (tok * m).sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e) / m.sum(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e).clamp(min=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1.0\u003c/span\u003e)","        mx = tok.masked_fill(~mask[..., \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e], float(\u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;-inf\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e)).amax(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","        mx = torch.where(","            torch.isfinite(mx), mx, torch.zeros_like(mx)","        )  \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# all-masked row -\u0026gt; 0\u003c/span\u003e","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-builtin\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e.to_token(torch.cat([mean, mx], dim=-\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e))[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e, :]","","","\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-definition\"\u003e_self_check\u003c/span\u003e():","    torch.manual_seed(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e)","    enc = KappaSetEncoder(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e32\u003c/span\u003e, n_probes=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e, p_drop=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e0.3\u003c/span\u003e).eval()","    b, P = \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e","    probes = torch.stack(","        [torch.arange(P).float(), torch.rand(P), torch.rand(P).round()], -\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e","    )[\u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e].repeat(b, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e)","    mask = torch.ones(b, P, dtype=torch.bool)","    out = enc((probes, mask))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e out.shape == (b, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e32\u003c/span\u003e), out.shape","    perm = torch.randperm(P)","    out_p = enc((probes[:, perm], mask[:, perm]))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e torch.allclose(out, out_p, atol=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-5\u003c/span\u003e), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;not permutation invariant\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# mask handling: masking probe 3 == physically removing it\u003c/span\u003e","    mask2 = mask.clone()","    mask2[:, \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e] = \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e","    keep = [i \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e i \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e range(P) \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e i != \u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e]","    a = enc((probes, mask2))","    c = enc((probes[:, keep], mask[:, keep]))","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e torch.allclose(a, c, atol=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-5\u003c/span\u003e), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;masked probe leaks into the token\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e torch.allclose(a, out, atol=\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e1e-3\u003c/span\u003e), \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;removing a probe changed nothing\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-comment\"\u003e# training drop never empties a row\u003c/span\u003e","    enc.train()","    \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e _ \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e range(\u003cspan class=\"tok-number\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e):","        o = enc((probes, mask))","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-keyword\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e torch.isfinite(o).all()","    print(","        \u003cspan class=\"tok-string\"\u003e\u0026quot;ok KappaSetEncoder: shape (b,1,dim), permutation-invariant, mask == removal, drop finite\u0026quot;\u003c/span\u003e","    )"],"symbols":[{"name":"obj_feat_dim","start":99,"end":100},{"name":"object_features","start":103,"end":138},{"name":"SceneEncoder","start":144,"end":165},{"name":"SceneEncoder.__init__","start":147,"end":161},{"name":"SceneEncoder.forward","start":163,"end":165},{"name":"grow_scene_channels","start":168,"end":203},{"name":"MetricSceneEncoder","start":206,"end":231},{"name":"MetricSceneEncoder.__init__","start":219,"end":227},{"name":"MetricSceneEncoder.forward","start":229,"end":231},{"name":"edge_deltas_torch","start":246,"end":261},{"name":"perception_input","start":264,"end":276},{"name":"FiLM","start":279,"end":297},{"name":"FiLM.__init__","start":289,"end":293},{"name":"FiLM.forward","start":295,"end":297},{"name":"PerceptionEncoder","start":300,"end":347},{"name":"PerceptionEncoder.__init__","start":310,"end":331},{"name":"PerceptionEncoder.forward","start":333,"end":347},{"name":"CapabilityEncoder","start":354,"end":361},{"name":"CapabilityEncoder.__init__","start":355,"end":357},{"name":"CapabilityEncoder.forward","start":359,"end":361},{"name":"SensitivityHead","start":364,"end":417},{"name":"SensitivityHead.forward","start":404,"end":417},{"name":"MorphCapabilityEncoder","start":420,"end":446},{"name":"MorphCapabilityEncoder.__init__","start":433,"end":441},{"name":"MorphCapabilityEncoder.forward","start":443,"end":446},{"name":"PhysicalCapabilityEncoder","start":449,"end":485},{"name":"PhysicalCapabilityEncoder.__init__","start":464,"end":480},{"name":"PhysicalCapabilityEncoder.forward","start":482,"end":485},{"name":"StructureEncoder","start":489,"end":496},{"name":"StructureEncoder.__init__","start":490,"end":491},{"name":"StructureEncoder.pool","start":493,"end":496},{"name":"KappaSetEncoder","start":500,"end":529},{"name":"KappaSetEncoder.__init__","start":501,"end":508},{"name":"KappaSetEncoder.forward","start":510,"end":529},{"name":"_self_check","start":532,"end":560}]}});
